  "_commit": {
    "id": "203a6efad7a3cfb5b007dc4aef5e5ce6ab380b28",
    "author": "Damian <damian.szk@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Damian <damian.szk@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Clearer values/ranks help: whole list, not a leading edge, score scale\n\nThe help pages now say what GSEA users could misread:\n- Give all measured proteins without a cutoff: the submitted list is the\n  background, so set_background does not apply and\n  number_of_genes_in_background is for information only.\n- inputGenes lists all of a term's proteins in the input, not a leading\n  edge; inputValues and inputRanks follow its order.\n- The rows are ordered by category, then FDR, as in get_enrichment; the\n  example sorts by FDR.\n- Give signed values (log fold changes, t statistics), not p-values.\n- enrichment_score follows STRING's definition (0 to 10, no sign), and\n  the KS and AFC tests are described as STRING chooses them.\n- The STRING v11 paper is the reference for the method. The pages show\n  how to save the list columns with write.csv, say to keep the job ids\n  for another R session, and to keep the API key private.\n\n?map and ?get_enrichment now open (plain aliases), and the values/ranks\npages link to the pages they mention.\n",
    "time": 1793965318
  },
